+# P0–P7 closeout ledger — research-only independent probe
+
+Date: 2026-10-31. All project-level `blocker_closed` values remain **false**.
+
+| Gate | Executed in this kit | Scope actually supported | Remaining blocker / next action |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P0 shared semantics | Independent, strict `u32` SSA verifier and parser, checked/wrap semantics, adversarial tests | One block; research JSON schema separate from canonical HIA | Compare exact SHA/version against `hepta.hia_opcodes`, `hia_schema`, `hia_program`, Python VM, Rust verifier and LLVM; generate one registry and versioned adapters; run canonical source-bound tests |
+| P1 resources and failures | Straight-line owner/loan/static peak payload, negative alias/double-drop cases; checked arithmetic with explicit overflow/div-zero/shift traps and real native status ABI | Straight line, no host crash/cancellation, true heap RSS or native stack bound | Prove whole control-flow borrow and cleanup; allocator failure schedule, trap ledger, cooperative cancel, interruption, parallelism; independent Rust and formal checks |
+| P2 real ABI | Actual GCC + Clang generated shared objects and C/C++ C ABI executable consumer on local machine | Host-specific `u32` ABI, C++ demo; 32-bit unsigned assumption asserted | x86-64 and AArch64 system ABI, cross-compiler/native artifacts, layouts, complete back-end refinement, physical device test |
+| P3 `c2hepta` | Clang AST source to standalone strict research u32 Core; original C vs generated C/VM differential | Single unsigned-return C function and supported scalar operators, no macros/includes/global/calls/control flow | Replace/prove against canonical translator, real maintained existing C project, original headers/build/clients, upstream upgrade, fault injection, measured human time |
+| P4 C++ | Real Clang++/G++ toy C++ RAII, exception, stale-handle, C ABI call | Demo component, one session, no real external library | Migrate actual version-pinned C++ dependency, upstream upgrade, exception/RTTI/template/inheritance cases, record engineering hours |
+| P5 global optimizer | Finite oracle+DP, full seven-component declared one-time costs, abstention when no positive benefit | Synthetic accounting, not actual optimized Hepta/Rust timings | Freeze prospective workloads; benchmark optimized Rust and Clang LTO/PGO; verify e-graph/SMT transforms; prove *real* positive full net benefit |
+| P6 NDU value | Same-information fixed, greedy, exact DP, exhaustive experimental controls; `native_ndu=UNAVAILABLE` | Does NOT run original Rust NDU or native bridge | Reconnect original Rust NDU `evaluate_recursive_utility` and `evaluate_candidates_with_policy`; same candidates/info/budgets, independently measured controller cost, prospective holdout |
+| P7 production/Agents | Full test log and artifact hash inventory for this probe | Offline toy profiles only | Rust/Lean/Agent fresh hidden tasks, actual maintenance costs, RSS/p95/p99, real CPU/GPU/AArch64, crash/restart/rollback, production version gate, independent audit |
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+This kit is an **advisory test input**. Its receipts carry `DENY_ALL` and cannot prove/authorize arbitrary transformed binaries. The separate Hepta canonical admission authority must verify every actual Core, invocation, target and artifact at the time of execution. A verified digest, by itself, does not authenticate who verified it.
+
+## Highest-priority integration actions when access returns
+
+1. Freeze *current* main and HIA active candidate HEADs and exact toolchains. Do not assume last session's `125d11c5454835a7df1dc51915fc49901fbede5b` main or `3201298a9828927452d42bcac146e610e1348a7f` candidate remains current.
+2. Check the new probe against the existing instruction contracts; any contradictory behavior must produce **REJECT**, not silently change the production Core. Do not add a second public compiler.
+3. Integrate only independently useful regression cases into existing canonical tests/validators; preserve original P0–P7 evidence and current active stacks.
+4. Run exact-head Rust/LLVM/source migration tests and native ABI qualification on x86-64 and AArch64.
+5. Register real unseen workload baselines and the full optimization cost ledger **before** candidate selection; use the original native NDU, fixed, DP and exhaustive controls.
+6. Only mark a blocker closed with source-bound independently reproducible receipts. Negative advantages remain negative and do not block documenting partial technical progress.
+
